-- title:
--   Factoring a power series with distinct linear lowest form
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field and $\iota$ a finite type, and let $a, b : \iota \to \kappa$ be families of scalars such that for all $i \neq j$ one has $a_i b_j - a_j b_i \neq 0$, i.e. the linear forms $a_i X_0 + b_i X_1$ are pairwise non-proportional. Write $\mathfrak m = (X_0, X_1)$ for the ideal of $\kappa[[X_0, X_1]] =$ `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) κ` generated by the two variables. Suppose $f \in \kappa[[X_0, X_1]]$ satisfies $$f - \prod_{i \in \iota} \bigl(C(a_i) X_0 + C(b_i) X_1\bigr) \in \mathfrak m^{\,|\iota| + 1},$$ where $|\iota|$ is the cardinality of $\iota$ and $C$ denotes the constant-coefficient inclusion $\kappa \to \kappa[[X_0,X_1]]$. Then there exist a family $L : \iota \to \kappa[[X_0, X_1]]$ and an element $w \in \kappa[[X_0,X_1]]$ such that $w$ is a unit, each $L_i$ satisfies $L_i - (C(a_i) X_0 + C(b_i) X_1) \in \mathfrak m^2$, and $f = w \cdot \prod_{i \in \iota} L_i$. Note that the non-proportionality hypothesis is imposed for all pairs $i \neq j$, so it also forces $(a_i, b_i) \neq (0,0)$ as soon as $|\iota| \geq 2$, whereas for $|\iota| \le 1$ the zero form is permitted.
--
--   This is a form of Hensel's lemma for the $\mathfrak m$-adic (total degree) filtration of the two-variable power series ring: a series whose lowest-degree form is a product of pairwise distinct lines through the origin factors into branches, one for each line, up to a unit. It is used in the analysis of local charts on Drinfeld curves, where it produces the branch primes and the discrete valuation rings attached to them from a congruence of a local equation with a product of linear forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_isUnit_mul_prod_eq_of_sub_prod_linear_mem_pow.lean

